Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:30:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Bound the barycentric builder's orphan-repair query

The repair gave each orphan coarse DOF its nearest unclaimed fine DOF from one
kd-tree query of orphans + 8 neighbours for every orphan, an (orphans x orphans)
array: the #893 blow-up (8.6 GB per rank at 121 s, stacks at custom_mg.py:164-165,
fixed for the parallel route by #890). The serial custom-FMG route, the legacy
set_custom_mg path and the public default (repair_orphans=True) still ran it.

The query now starts at 9 neighbours and doubles for one orphan only while every
candidate is already claimed. The claims are the same: orphans are taken in the
same order and each takes the first unclaimed candidate in the same distance
order. Checked bit-identical against development's builder on every call in the
custom-MG and placed-ribbon test files (98 calls), on K1's #893 fixture at
refinement 4 (orphans 10 and 38), and on 40 random 2-D/3-D clouds.

test_1015_custom_mg_orphan_repair_memory forces 1,770 orphans; development's
builder peaks at 55 MB there (fails the 20 MB cap), this one at 4 MB.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
